.page group 5 the group database

# DESCRIPTION
`/Hakurei/etc/group` lists the groups, one per line, in four fields separated by colons:

    name:password:gid:member,member,...

The members are the users who belong to the group in addition to their primary group, which is given by the fourth field of passwd(5). The shipped file has a group for each resident and the shared group `shrine`:

    root:x:0:root
    reimu:x:1000:reimu
    marisa:x:1001:marisa
    sakuya:x:1002:sakuya
    sumireko:x:1003:sumireko
    shrine:x:100:reimu,marisa,sakuya

`shrine` (gid 100) is the **seat** group. Its members may use the display and input devices (`/dev/fb0`, `/dev/input/events`), which is what running the desktop takes, and may restart or power off the machine. Everyone except Sumireko, an outsider, belongs to it. A user outside `shrine` gets the text console only, and `poweroff` answers *Operation not permitted*.

# SEE ALSO
passwd(5), adduser(8), id(1), groups(1), accounts(7)
